      "math_academy_id": "q-35217",
      "knowledge_point_id": "40a70c8d-dc8e-52bd-a679-ffd6d1940451",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Inverse of a Function With a Parameter",
      "problem": "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=ax-7$, where $a$ is a non-zero constant.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=ax-7\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=ay-7\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =ay-7 \\\\ x+7 & =ay \\\\ \\frac{x+7}{a} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+7}{a}\n$$",
