  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932636",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-101587",
      "knowledge_point_id": "bb40a0ff-c3b5-512d-a436-cc2fce456008",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Exponential Function, Plus a Constant",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=5{e}^{x}+1$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of ${e}^{x}$ is just ${e}^{x}$ itself. On the other hand, $1$ is a constant, so its derivative is $0.$\n\nFirst, using the addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{e}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+0 \\\\  & =5{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=0} & ={(5{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=0} \\\\  & =5{e}^{0} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "5",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-1",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "1",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "0",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "ln⁡5",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "provenance": {
        "activity_question": "question-101587",
        "kp_title": "Differentiating the Product of a Constant and the Exponential Function, Plus a Constant",
        "kp_href": null
      },
      "topic_id": 1114,
