      "knowledge_point": "Computing the Mean of a Data Set From the Sum",
      "problem": "Given a data set with $23$ data points and ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{23}{x}_{i}=590,$ compute $\\overset{―}{x}.$ Round your answer to one decimal place.",
      "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the mean is denoted by $\\overset{―}{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=23$ and ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{23}{x}_{i}=590,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{23}\\cdot 590≈25.7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have rounded our answer to one decimal place.",
