    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-160052",
      "knowledge_point_id": "adfc527d-4347-5741-a81c-fa91c50d5d74",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing the Mean of a Data Set",
      "problem": "A college basketball player scored the following number of points in the last five games he played:\n\n$$\n9,\\,11,\\,12,\\,8,\\,10\n$$\n\nWhat is the mean of these scores?",
      "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$ then the mean is denoted by $\\overset{―}{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\n$$\n\nHere, there are $n=5$ data points. Adding up all the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i} & =9+11+12+8+10 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 50 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
